// XFAIL: RT-323b: (RT-323's mechanism, the projection inside the alias) a module-level `type V = Option<<S as A>::Out>;` is refused (trait.unmet "'S' has no impl of 'A' that defines 'Out'"), while the same type written in a `let` builds; rustc prints true true 2 (0.30.2)
// From the paused g302qual work (PAUSED.md, findings not mine, 2): an
// item-level projection is read before the impls are known (RT-355 a
// struct field's, RT-323 and RT-170 an alias that is the projection
// itself). Since v0.30.1 at least (the same error).
// EXPECT: true true 2
trait A {
    type Out;
}

trait B {
    const D: i64;
}

struct S;

struct O;

impl A for S {
    type Out = O;
}

impl B for O {
    const D: i64 = 2;
}

type V = Option<<S as A>::Out>;

fn main() {
    let v: V = None;
    let w: Option<<S as A>::Out> = Some(O);
    println("{} {} {}", v.is_none(), w.is_some(), <O as B>::D);
}
